# What never belongs in the image. The rule is section 0 of doc/STORAGE.md:
# an image ships CODE, state lives on a mounted volume and outlives the
# container. Anything below is either state, or weight with no runtime use.

# State. /data is a mount point, never a layer — copying it in would freeze a
# snapshot of the ledgers into the image and hide the fact that the container
# is writing somewhere that dies with it.
data/
models/
catboost_info/

# History and tooling
.git/
.gitignore
.claude/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# 1.3 MB of notebooks and 794 KB of PDF: analysis artifacts, read by people,
# never by the cycle, and the only files here heavy enough to be worth a line.
*.ipynb
*.pdf

# The markdown stays. It is ~250 KB, `features.py --fields-doc` actually reads
# FIELDS.md, and an image that can explain itself (`docker run ... cat
# doc/RUNBOOK.md`) is worth more than the layer it costs.
